+# VCF 9.1 architecture research record
+
+The pinned local snapshot remains the artifact authority where live material is newer or differently scoped. Coverage includes VMware Aria Suite Lifecycle, VMware Aria Operations, VMware Aria Automation, VMware Aria Operations for Logs, VMware Live Site Recovery, VMware NSX, VMware vCenter Server, VMware ESXi, and VMware vSAN.
+
+- **Upgrade sequence and related issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed that estates with NSX 4.x and Aria Automation use VCF Installer converge/import rather than independent component upgrades, and that Operations precedes convergence.
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed management-product ordering, core ordering, the Aria Suite Lifecycle transition patch, and fresh deployment rather than in-place upgrade for Logs 8.x.
+- **NSX 9.x is only supported as part of a VCF 9.x environment** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/401775/nsx-9x-is-only-supported-as-part-of-a-vc.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed that standalone NSX 4.x must be imported into VCF before its 9.x upgrade.
+- **vCenter upgrade precheck from version 8.x to 9.x failing due to NSX version** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425164/vcenter-upgrade-precheck-from-version-8x.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed the VCF-managed interoperability exception and the need to import the NSX-backed environment before upgrading vCenter.
+- **VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1: Transition from standalone SRM and VR 9.0.2** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/vcf-protection-and-recovery-91-transitio.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed that the 9.0.2 recovery appliances must transition to the unified 9.1 architecture, normally converging through 9.0.4, before the vCenter 9.1 target.
+- **Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Cross-checked the product/version pairings and upgrade-path view for vCenter, ESXi, vSAN, NSX, and Live Site Recovery without treating the mutable live matrix as the grading oracle.
+- **VCF Operations 9.0 Sizing Guidelines** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/397782/vcf-operations-90-sizing-guidelines.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Cross-checked Operations node sizing and HA constraints and the published Operations for Logs ingestion profiles; used the seed's pinned profiles for deterministic output.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) Operations Sizing Guidelines** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/324340/vmware-cloud-foundation-vcf-operations-s.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed the version-routed sizing guidance for Operations 8.18 through 9.1.
+- **Aria Operations for Logs Sizing Calculator** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/344251/vrealize-log-insight-sizing-calculator.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed that ingestion and retention both drive Logs sizing.
+- **How to log into the Log Management UI in VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article?articleNumber=442141 — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed that VCF 9.1 Log Management is integrated into VCF Operations and runs in the VCF Management Services Platform.
+- **Scaling down your VCF 9 environment** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/434650/scaling-down-your-vcf-9-environment.html — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed VCF Automation's scale-up/scale-out lifecycle model; the selected pinned profile fits the fixture demand without relying on a later scale-down.
+- **vmware/vcf-api-specs tag 9.1.0.0, VCF Installer OpenAPI** — https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed `SddcSpec`, its native VCF Operations and Automation fields, and management-infrastructure fields.
+- **vmware/vcf-api-specs Apache License 2.0** — https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/LICENSE — Accessed 2026-08-14 — Confirmed the license of the pinned installer specification shipped with the fixture.
